WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.380
New to the gym? Here's what all those words mean, so you can walk in and know what to do.

2
00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:15.127
A rep is one lift, up and down. Like one squat.

3
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:20.013
A set is a group of reps, done back to back.

4
00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:24.043
Three by eight means three sets of eight reps.

5
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.193
Pick a weight where the last rep or two feel hard, while your form still holds.

6
00:00:30.543 --> 00:00:34.703
When you're not sure, go lighter. You can always add more next set.

7
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.860
Rest about one to three minutes between sets.

8
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.250
In RepBunny, the rest timer starts for you.

9
00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:47.387
RPE is how hard a set felt, from one to ten.

10
00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:51.257
If you could have done about two more reps, that's an eight.

11
00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:53.527
Logging it is optional.

12
00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:56.493
A few words you'll hear.

13
00:00:56.843 --> 00:01:00.283
A warm-up set is a lighter set, to get loose.

14
00:01:00.633 --> 00:01:04.713
A PR is a personal record, your best ever.

15
00:01:05.063 --> 00:01:08.983
And progressive overload just means adding a little over time.

16
00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:13.443
Now let's log a set in RepBunny. Type the weight you lifted,

17
00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.553
and how many reps.

18
00:01:15.904 --> 00:01:18.144
Then tap the Add set button.

19
00:01:18.496 --> 00:01:22.336
That's one set done! Tap the Nice button to keep going.
